  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2022-05-06T20:41:03.221Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "# Summary\nClicking a window size (i. e. `1280x720`) affects the Creator Companion window differently if the user uses different Window scale settings on each monitor. (i. e. 100% and 150%).\n# Details\nThe 'window size' setting allows us to change the size of the `CreatorCompanion.exe` window.\nHowever, the scaling of the monitor on which the window is display affects the outcome of the 'window size' setting. If both monitors share the same scaling (i. e. 100%), the issue does not occur.\nHere's an annotated album to illustrate the issue: https://imgur.com/a/6QjqrfT\nI assume that my previously reported bugs might be related to this.\n(Sorry about reporting so many multi-monitor issues! 🙏)",
